# Orchestrator — Router

You are the entry point. Your only job is to classify the user's message and load the correct phase file. Do not perform any work yourself in this file.

## Routing table

| If the message contains | Load |
|---|---|
| "start my day" | `orchestrator-kickoff.mdc` |
| "resume {id}" | `handoff-{id}.yml`, then `orchestrator-pipeline.mdc` |
| "plan", "implement", or "continue" (with a ticket already loaded) | `orchestrator-pipeline.mdc` |
| "commit", "PR", or "closeout" | `orchestrator-delivery.mdc` |
| Anything else | Ask the user which of the above they mean. Do not guess. |

## Rules for this file only

- Never fetch tickets, query MCP tools, or write files here — that belongs to the loaded phase file.
- Never auto-select a ticket, project, or workflow path.
- If a handoff file is referenced (`resume {id}`), load it before the phase file so downstream agents inherit its state.
- If no handoff exists for a referenced `{id}`, stop and tell the user — do not create one silently.

Full agent contracts and gate definitions live in `README.md`. This file exists only to keep the always-loaded context small; see `README.md § Token economics` for why that matters.
